# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# iBarangay — Docker Environment File
#
# ── OPTION A: Run instantly with the demo Firebase project (zero setup) ───────
#
#   The app already has working Firebase credentials hardcoded as fallbacks
#   in src/firebase/config.ts pointing to the developers project.
#   You can run the app immediately WITHOUT filling this file:
#
#     docker compose up --build
#     open http://localhost:3000
#
#   Login with any of the demo accounts or visit /initial-setup.
#   NOTE: In this mode you are sharing the developer's Firebase database.
#
# ── OPTION B: Use your own Firebase project (full isolation) ─────────────────
#
#   STEP 1  Copy this file:
#             cp .env.docker.example .env.docker
#
#   STEP 2  Fill in YOUR Firebase credentials below (see HOW TO GET below).
#
#   STEP 3  Build & run with the env file:
#             docker compose --env-file .env.docker up --build
#             open http://localhost:3000
#
#   STEP 4  First-time setup: visit http://localhost:3000/initial-setup
#           to create the Super Admin account on your Firebase project.
#
#   NEVER commit .env.docker — it is already in .gitignore.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Firebase Client SDK (browser-side) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Source: Firebase Console → Project Settings → Your Apps → Web app → Config
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project-id.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project-id.appspot.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=000000000000
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX


# ── Firebase Admin SDK (server-side) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Source: Firebase Console → Project Settings → Service Accounts
#         → "Generate new private key" → open downloaded JSON → copy values
#
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@your-project-id.iam.gserviceaccount.com
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nYour private key content here\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"


# ── Google Gemini AI (optional — AI Insights feature) ────────────────────────
# Source: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Leave blank to disable AI — the rest of the app works fine without it.
#
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO GET FIREBASE VALUES (Option B only)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com and create (or select) a project
#  2. Enable: Authentication (Email/Password), Firestore, Storage
#
#  Client SDK values (NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_*):
#    Project Settings → Your Apps → Web app → firebaseConfig object
#
#  Admin SDK values:
#    Project Settings → Service Accounts → Generate new private key
#    Open the downloaded JSON:
#      FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID   = project_id
#      FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL = client_email
#      FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY  = private_key (keep quotes, keep \n characters)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
